# Map fixture directories to spec sections.
#
# Format: <dir-relative-to-compiler-root>     <spec-section-tag>
#
# The sync-test-links.sh script reads this file to know which spec
# subsection's <!-- BEGIN tests:X.Y --> ... <!-- END tests:X.Y --> block
# should list the runtime-discovered tests for a fixture directory.
#
# Section tags use the form FILE-SLUG:SECTION_TAG when the section is in a
# doc other than LANGUAGE.md. e.g. "format-snapshot" lives in FORMATTER.md
# under <!-- BEGIN tests:format-snapshot -->. A bare tag like "16.7" lives
# in LANGUAGE.md.
#
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.

tests/scenarios            16.8
tests/format               format-snapshot
tests/corpus/valid         16.10
tests/corpus/invalid       16.10
tests/corpus/snapshot      16.10
